      "classification": "potential-vulnerability",
      "code_path": "sui-move-contract/contracts/protocol/sources/internal/referral.move::update_referral_params::L244-256",
      "proof_trace": "The sum invariant (referrer_bps + referee_bps < 10000) is not enforced: update_referral_params validates each bps individually against DENOMINATOR (L250-251) but never checks their combined sum, allowing e.g. referrer=9000 + referee=9000=18000 to pass. The sequential computation in track_flash_loan_usage (L132-138) prevents arithmetic overflow (referrer receives a fraction of the fee remaining after referee's share, so total rebates always < initial_fee), but the stored invariant is violated and the protocol could be configured to retain near-zero flash loan fees.",
      "attack_scenario": "An AdminCap holder (or compromised admin key) calls update_referral_params with referrer_discount_bps=9000 and referee_discount_bps=9000; subsequently every flash loan distributes ~99% of its fee as rebates (90% to referee, then 90% of remaining to referrer), leaving the protocol with ~1% of fee revenue.",
      "checklist_id": "PROP-01b-partial-inv-034"
    },
    "text": "Referral rebate percentages (referrer + referee) must not exceed 100% of the fee.",
    "assertion": "forall referral r: r.referrer_discount_bps + r.referee_discount_bps < 10000",
    "covers": "SG-022",
    "severity": "MEDIUM",
    "type": "invariant"
  }
}

